"""
Authentication is intentionally REST-only.

Login, signup, refresh and logout live at `/api/v1/auth/*`. They are
credential-handling endpoints that need to set precise HTTP status codes,
participate in rate-limit accounting per outcome, and be trivially auditable
in an access log — none of which GraphQL's single-endpoint, always-200 model
expresses well. A GraphQL client authenticates by presenting the access token
those endpoints issue:

    Authorization: Bearer <access token>

The same JWT middleware validates it for both transports.
"""
